    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg–Turing wavelength for Fractofusus misrai at 63 µm (565 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 84.9/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Detail-scale (tier 4_cellular_10um) Schnakenberg field whose analytical critical wavelength is fixed at 6.33e-05 m (63 µm, log10 = -4.199) for the 565 Ma Mistaken Point chronospecies, series index 1/1. Spectral growth rates match the Turing dispersion relation (Pearson r = 0.999999999, RMSE = 0.00375) for integer k = 1..8. The saturated field's dominant wavelength is 73.7 µm, a disclosed nonlinear shift away from the linear 63.3 µm. D_u from 0.05 to 0.25 lengthens analytical λ_c monotonically. Equal diffusion and a 2×2 subcritical domain both decay. The CC BY 2.0 Mistaken Point photograph is segmented (spindle aspect 1.70) and compared with the rendered spindle (aspect 1.11); gradient-angle KS D = 0.093. Fifty-one of these wavelengths fit in the 3.275 mm organ-scale module and fifty-two do not. The 63 µm length is the evaluation scale, not a published thin-section measurement. Overall 84.9/100 (faithfulness 84.1, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 726931 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 764499f45bf6c5c2be034bc5a534df51a43eb1cfe24db598fe40d9c0f486fac2 (sha256 764499f45bf6c5c2be034bc5a534df51a43eb1cfe24db598fe40d9c0f486fac2), spec_fingerprint b7aed75670ec58eb2e24b6b33d4964b84814f0e27b8d16305477ab4160932f43. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b7aed75670ec58eb2e24b6b33d4964b84814f0e27b8d16305477ab4160932f43; artifact_sha256: 764499f45bf6c5c2be034bc5a534df51a43eb1cfe24db598fe40d9c0f486fac2; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=749222e73e20900f..., datasets/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0/fractofusus_misrai_specimen.jpg=e423fba39900f0b8..., datasets/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=6b331d726b68779e..., datasets/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=365f45ca2b96a3cb..., datasets/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=00bdda7655784bfa...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a homogeneous reaction-diffusion state can be unstable at a finite critical wavenumber k_c, selecting a stationary wavelength. | Gehling & Narbonne 2007 name Fractofusus misrai from Mistaken Point and place it in the mid-Ediacaran, ca. 575–560 Ma, as a fusiform rangeomorph below the photic zone. | Hoyal Cuthill & Conway Morris 2014: rangeomorph fronds are a fractal, self-similar, axial-apical-alternate body plan consistent with osmotrophy. | Mitchell et al. 2015: Fractofusus spatial clusters record multigenerational stolon-like reproduction plus waterborne propagules.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters a=0.09, b=0.85, D_u=0.12, D_v=2.40, with the grid spacing chosen so analytical λ_c = 6.33e-05 m. These constants are not taken from slot 1251. | A siltstone-coloured spindle render whose interior contrast is the growing activator. Chevron ridges are a display of the selected wavelength, not a measured branch angle.; transfer_boundary: The wavenumber law is evaluated at 63 µm on one Mistaken Point bedding-plane photograph. It does not transfer to Fractofusus andersoni, to the 3.275 mm organ-scale module, or to Cambrian bilaterian segmentation.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured 63 µm pigment ocellus or cellular reaction-diffusion stripe on Fractofusus. Mistaken Point preserves external moulds. | Does not claim the saturated 73.7 µm Fourier peak equals the linear wavelength. The shift is reported. | Does not claim a second chronospecies. The series is 1/1 at 565 Ma.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Measure the saturated-field Fourier wavelength at each D_u in the sweep, not only the analytical λ_c.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': \"The render's interior reads as a spot lattice. Weight oblique rangeomorph vanes more strongly than the raw spots and re-score the GIF against the specimen.\"}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Single assessor. A second provider has not scored this pass.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.49e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg–Turing wavelength for Fractofusus misrai at 63 µm (565 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Raising D_u from 0.05 to 0.25 lengthens analytical λ_c monotonically from about 40 µm to about 93 µm, and the sweep is plotted. Equal diffusion and a domain shorter than λ_c both lose the pattern. The sweep is still analytical: the saturated field's own Fourier wavelength has been measured only at the nominal D_u." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

