<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg–Turing wavelength for Fractofusus misrai at 63 µm (565 Ma) (Fractofusus misrai (Ediacaran spindle rangeomorph))",
        "Schnakenberg–Turing wavelength for Fractofusus misrai at 63 µm (565 Ma) faithfully reproduces Fractofusus misrai (Ediacaran spindle rangeomorph) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Fractofusus misrai (Ediacaran spindle rangeomorph) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Fractofusus misrai (Ediacaran spindle rangeomorph)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured 63 µm pigment ocellus or cellular reaction-diffusion stripe on Fractofusus. Mistaken Point preserves external moulds.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim a second chronospecies. The series is 1/1 at 565 Ma.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the saturated 73.7 µm Fourier peak equals the linear wavelength. The shift is reported.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: A siltstone-coloured spindle render whose interior contrast is the growing activator. Chevron ridges are a display of the selected wavelength, not a measured branch angle.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters a=0.09, b=0.85, D_u=0.12, D_v=2.40, with the grid spacing chosen so analytical λ_c = 6.33e-05 m. These constants are not taken from slot 1251.",
        "reported_in_source: Gehling & Narbonne 2007 name Fractofusus misrai from Mistaken Point and place it in the mid-Ediacaran, ca. 575–560 Ma, as a fusiform rangeomorph below the photic zone.",
        "reported_in_source: Hoyal Cuthill & Conway Morris 2014: rangeomorph fronds are a fractal, self-similar, axial-apical-alternate body plan consistent with osmotrophy.",
        "reported_in_source: Mitchell et al. 2015: Fractofusus spatial clusters record multigenerational stolon-like reproduction plus waterborne propagules.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a homogeneous reaction-diffusion state can be unstable at a finite critical wavenumber k_c, selecting a stationary wavelength.",
        "transfer_boundary: The wavenumber law is evaluated at 63 µm on one Mistaken Point bedding-plane photograph. It does not transfer to Fractofusus andersoni, to the 3.275 mm organ-scale module, or to Cambrian bilaterian segmentation." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Fractofusus misrai (Late Ediacaran (Newfoundland, 565 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Zoophyta & Vermes (Cnidaria/Platyhelminthes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Fractofusus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Fractofusus misrai (Ediacaran spindle rangeomorph); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a homogeneous reaction-diffusion state can be unstable at a finite critical wavenumber k_c, selecting a stationary wavelength. | Gehling & Narbonne 2007 name Fractofusus misrai from Mistaken Point and place it in the mid-Ediacaran, ca. 575–560 Ma, as a fusiform rangeomorph below the photic zone. | Hoyal Cuthill & Conway Morris 2014: rangeomorph fronds are a fractal, self-similar, axial-apical-alternate body plan consistent with osmotrophy. | Mitchell et al. 2015: Fractofusus spatial clusters record multigenerational stolon-like reproduction plus waterborne propagules.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters a=0.09, b=0.85, D_u=0.12, D_v=2.40, with the grid spacing chosen so analytical λ_c = 6.33e-05 m. These constants are not taken from slot 1251. | A siltstone-coloured spindle render whose interior contrast is the growing activator. Chevron ridges are a display of the selected wavelength, not a measured branch angle.; transfer_boundary: The wavenumber law is evaluated at 63 µm on one Mistaken Point bedding-plane photograph. It does not transfer to Fractofusus andersoni, to the 3.275 mm organ-scale module, or to Cambrian bilaterian segmentation.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured 63 µm pigment ocellus or cellular reaction-diffusion stripe on Fractofusus. Mistaken Point preserves external moulds. | Does not claim the saturated 73.7 µm Fourier peak equals the linear wavelength. The shift is reported. | Does not claim a second chronospecies. The series is 1/1 at 565 Ma.]; phenomenon_size: 66 µm (6.55e-05 m, log10=-4.184 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 66 µm to 14.7 cm): 66 µm:fractofusus-misrai-bioelectric-polarity, 205 µm:fractofusus-misrai-vertex-packing, 3.3 mm:fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength, 6.6 mm:fractofusus-misrai-clock-wavefront, 1.5 cm:fractofusus-misrai-morphogen-condensation, 1.8 cm:fractofusus-misrai-elastic-buckling, 2.0 cm:fractofusus-misrai-flux-canalization, 2.9 cm:fractofusus-misrai-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature14646>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1408542111>,
